---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
// TODO: set this to the date you publish or change the policy.
const updated = 'October 6, 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Solo Spark"
  description="How Solo Spark LLC handles the information you send through the mysolospark.com contact form, including how Web3Forms delivers it."
>
  <PageHero title="Privacy policy" lede={`Last updated ${updated}.`} />

  <section class="section-y pt-12!">
    <div class="page-x">
      <div class="prose-ss">
        <p>
          This policy explains what {site.legalName} ("Solo Spark", "I", "me") collects through
          {' '}<a href={site.url}>mysolospark.com</a> and what I do with it. I keep it short because I collect very little.
        </p>

        <h2>What I collect</h2>
        <p>When you send the contact form, I receive:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>your name,</li>
          <li>your email address,</li>
          <li>your company name, if you give it,</li>
          <li>your message about what you want to automate.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The site doesn't use cookies for tracking, advertising or analytics, and it doesn't ask you to create an account.
          Like most websites, the server that hosts this site may keep standard technical logs (such as IP address and
          browser type) for security and reliability.
        </p>

        <h2>How the contact form works</h2>
        <p>
          The form is delivered by <a href="https://web3forms.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Web3Forms</a>, a
          form-to-email service. When you press send, your entries go to Web3Forms, which forwards them to my email
          inbox. Web3Forms processes that data under its own
          {' '}<a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The form also contains a hidden field that people never see. If it's filled in, I treat the submission as
          spam and don't send it.
        </p>

        <h2>How I use your information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>to reply to your message,</li>
          <li>to talk with you about a possible project,</li>
          <li>to keep a record of our conversation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>I don't sell your information, and I don't add you to a mailing list.</p>

        <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
        <p>
          I keep messages in my email for as long as they're useful for our conversation or any work we do together.
          You can ask me to delete them at any time.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask to see, correct or delete the information you sent me. Email
          {' '}<a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a> and I'll take care of it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If this policy changes, I'll update it on this page and change the date at the top.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          {site.legalName}<br />
          {site.location.city}, {site.location.region}<br />
          <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a><br />
          <a href={site.contact.phoneHref}>{site.contact.phone}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
